hadiths[39]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3645","[AI-translation] Khattab regarding His saying: ""And when the girl [who was] buried alive is asked"" [At-Takwir: 8], he said: Qays bin 'Asim came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I buried eight daughters of mine in the pre-Islamic period. He said: Free a slave for each one of them. He said: I am a man of camels. He said: Then slaughter [in another narration: offer a sacrifice if you wish] a camel for each one."
"3646","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): The one who stabs himself, only stabs it in the Fire, and the one who plunges into it, plunges into the Fire, and the one who strangles himself, strangles it in the Fire."
"3647","[AI-translation] From Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not wrong the believer a good deed; he is rewarded for it with provision in this world and is recompensed for it in the Hereafter. As for the disbeliever, he is given for his good deeds in this world, so when he meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection, he will have no good deed for which he is given good."
"3648","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, stretches out His hand by night so that the sinner of the day may repent, and He stretches out His hand by day so that the sinner of the night may repent, until the sun rises from its west."
"3649","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Verily, Allah does not look at [your bodies, nor at] your forms and your wealth, but [rather] He looks at your hearts [and he pointed with his fingers to his chest] and your deeds."
"3650","On the authority of Amir bin Sa'd, he said: Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas was among his camels when his son Umar came to him. When Sa'd saw him, he said: ""I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of this rider."" So he dismounted and said to him: ""You stay among your camels and sheep and leave the people disputing over the kingdom among themselves?"" So Sa'd struck him on his chest and said: ""Be quiet! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'Indeed Allah loves the servant who is pious, wealthy, and inconspicuous.'""And Kathir bin Zayd al-Aslami narrated it from al-Mutallib from Umar bin Sa'd from his father that he said: His son Amir came to him and said: ""O my son! In the fitnah you command me to be a leader? No, by Allah! Until I am given a sword that if I strike a Muslim with it, it bounces off him, and if I strike a disbeliever with it, it kills him."" I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ... and he mentioned the hadith."
"3651","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was asked: Which deed is best? He said: That you bring joy to your believing brother, or pay off a debt for him, or feed him bread."
"3652","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: A man may have a rank with Allah which he does not attain by his deeds, so Allah continues to test him with what he dislikes until He causes him to reach it."
"3653","[AI-translation] Nu'man bin Bashir, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Verily, in the son of Adam is a morsel of flesh; when it is sound, the rest of his body is sound, and when it is corrupt, the rest of his body is corrupt. Verily, it is the heart."
"3654","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah bin 'Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The likeness of the one who commits evil deeds and then does righteous deeds is like a man upon whom was a tight coat of mail that was choking him; then he did a good deed and a ring was loosened, then he did another good deed and another ring was loosened, until it fell to the ground."
"3655","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah bin 'Amir, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The likeness of the one who commits evil deeds and then does righteous deeds is like a man upon whom was a tight coat of mail that was choking him; then he did a good deed and a ring was loosened, then he did another good deed and another ring was loosened, until it fell to the ground."
"3656","[AI-translation] From Abu Sa'id, who said: You certainly do deeds that are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, among the destructive sins."
"3657","[AI-translation] Ifk, he (peace be upon him) said: As for what follows! O 'Aishah! It has reached me concerning you such and such. [You are but of the daughters of Adam.] If you are innocent, then Allah will acquit you, and if you have committed a sin, then seek forgiveness from Allah and repent to Him, for when a servant confesses his sin and then repents to Allah, Allah accepts his repentance. And in a narration: Verily, repentance from the sin is regret."
"3658","[AI-translation] From 'Awf bin Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Beware of the sins that are not forgiven. (And in a narration: And the sins that have no expiation). Whoever misappropriates something will bring it on the Day of Resurrection, and the consumer of usury: whoever consumes usury will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a madman, convulsing. Then he recited: ""Those who consume usury will not stand except as one stands who is being beaten by Satan into madness."" (Al-Baqarah: 275)"
"3659","[AI-translation] From Sahl bin Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Beware of the belittled sins. (For the likeness of the belittled sins) is like a people who camped in the belly of a valley; one brought a stick, and another brought a stick, until they had baked their bread. And verily, the belittled sins, whenever their doer is seized for them, will destroy him."
"3660","[AI-translation] 'Abd Allah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Sin is the snare of the hearts, and there is no glance but that Satan has a desire in it."
"3661","[AI-translation] 'Ata' bin Yasar reported that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, sent Mu'adh to Yemen. He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Advise me."" He said: ""Fear Allah as much as you are able, and remember Allah at every stone and tree, and if you commit a bad deed, then offer repentance for it: secretly for a secret deed, and openly for an open deed."
"3662","On the authority of Sahl ibn al-Mu'tamir from al-Hujaymi: He said: I came to Medina and met the Prophet ﷺ in one of the alleyways of Medina. I found him wearing a cotton waist-wrapper whose hem had frayed. I said: ""Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""And upon you be peace, the greeting of the dead."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, advise me!"" He said: ""Do not belittle any good deed, even if it is giving the tie of a rope, or emptying from your bucket into the vessel of the one drawing water, or meeting your Muslim brother with a cheerful face, or comforting the lonely with your presence, or giving the shoelace."""
"3663","From Abu Tawil Shatab Al-Mamdud, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""What do you think of a man who committed all sins, leaving none of them, and in doing so he did not leave any need or desire except he fulfilled it. Is there any repentance for him?"" He said: ""Have you embraced Islam?"" He said: ""As for me, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone with no partner, and that you are the Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Yes, do good deeds and abandon evil deeds, and Allah will make them all good deeds for you."" He said: ""And my betrayals and immoral acts?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Allah is Greatest,"" and he did not cease saying Allahu Akbar until he disappeared from sight."
"3664","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah, the Exalted, said: If My servant loves to meet Me, I love to meet him; and if he dislikes meeting Me, I dislike meeting him."
"3665","[AI-translation] Ibn 'Abbas said: There was a man from the Ansar who embraced Islam, then apostatized and joined the polytheists. He then regretted it and sent word to his people: ""Ask the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, whether there is any repentance for me."" So his people came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and said: ""So-and-so has regretted, and he ordered us to ask you whether there is any repentance for him?"" Then was revealed: ""How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their faith..."" up to His words ""...Forgiving, Merciful"" (Aal 'Imran: 86). So he sent word to him, and he embraced Islam."
"3666","[AI-translation] Abu Dharr said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Be with the afflicted one in humility to your Lord and in faith."
"3667","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""The deed of none of you will enter him into Paradise."" [Nor will it save him from the Fire]. They said: ""Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Not even I, [and he gestured with his hand like this over his head], unless Allah encompasses me with His favor and mercy."" [He said this twice or thrice]. ""So be steadfast, draw near, and give glad tidings; go forth in the morning and evening, and journey a part of the night, and adhere to moderation, moderation, that you may attain. And know that the most beloved of deeds to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the most consistent, even if little."" It was reported from a group of the Companions..."
"3668","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Some people will wish they had committed more evil deeds. They said: ""Why, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Those whose evil deeds Allah has changed into good deeds."
"3669","[AI-translation] Ash'ari said: While he was teaching them something about the affairs of their religion, their eyes became fixed. He said: ""What made your eyes turn away from me?"" They said: ""We were looking at the moon."" He said: ""So how will it be for you when you see Allah directly?"
"3670","[AI-translation] 'Ubayd Allah bin Jarir reported from his father: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: There is no people among whom acts of disobedience are committed, being more numerous and mightier than those who commit them, and they do not change them, except that Allah is soon to encompass them with a punishment."
"3671","On the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out and saw a raised dome, so he said: ""What is this?"" His companions said to him: ""This belongs to so-and-so — a man from the Ansar."" He fell silent and held it against him inwardly, until when its owner came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeting him among the people, he turned away from him. He did this repeatedly. The man recognized the anger in him and the turning away, so he complained of that to his companions, saying: ""By Allah, I find the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed."" They said: ""He went out and saw your dome."" So the man returned to his dome and demolished it until he leveled it to the ground. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day and did not see it. He said: ""What happened to the dome?"" They said: ""Its owner complained to us of your turning away from him, so we informed him, and he demolished it."" He said: ""Know that every building is a burden upon its owner, except what... except what..."" — meaning what is absolutely necessary."
"3672","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever seeks the world harms the Hereafter, and whoever seeks the Hereafter harms the world! So harm the perishable for the sake of the everlasting."
"3673","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever seeks the world harms the Hereafter, and whoever seeks the Hereafter harms the world! So harm the fleeting for the sake of the everlasting."
"3674","[AI-translation] It was narrated from 'Alqamah bin Wa'il, from his father, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whoever unjustly seizes a man's land will meet Allah while He is angry with him."
"3675","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Thawban that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""Whosever soul departs his body while he is free of three things will enter Paradise: arrogance, debt, and Ghulul."
"3676","[AI-translation] Khudri that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, planted a stick in front of him, then planted another next to it, then planted a third and placed it further away. He then said: ""Do you know what this is?"" They said: ""Allah and His Messenger know best."" He said: ""This is the human being, this is his term, and this is his hope. He pursues his hope, but his term seizes him before that."
"3677","[AI-translation] Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by the ruins of a people in which there was a dead young goat. He said: ""Do its owners have any need for it?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If its owners had any need for it, they would not have discarded it."" He said: ""By Allah! The world is more insignificant to Allah than this young goat is to its owners. So let me not find that it has ruined any of you."
"3678","Dhayyal ibn Utbah ibn Hanzalah said: I heard Hanzalah ibn Hudhaym, my grandfather, [say] that his grandfather Hanifah said to Hudhaym: ""Gather my sons for me, for I wish to make a bequest."" So he gathered them, and he said: ""The first thing I bequest is that for this orphan of mine who is in my care [there shall be] one hundred camels from those camels which we used to call in the pre-Islamic period 'al-Mutayyibah' (the good/pure ones)."" Hudhaym said: ""O my father! I heard your sons saying: 'We only acknowledge this in our father's presence; when he dies, we will go back on it.'"" He said: ""Then between me and you is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" Hudhaym said: ""We are satisfied."" So Hudhaym, Hanifah, and Hanzalah set out with them, [along with] a boy who was riding behind Hudhaym. When they came to the Prophet ﷺ, they greeted him. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""What brought you here, O Abu Hudhaym?"" He said: ""This [matter],"" and he struck his hand on Hudhaym's thigh. He said: ""I feared that old age or death might overtake me suddenly, so I wanted to bequest that for this orphan of mine who is in my care one hundred camels from those camels which we used to call in the pre-Islamic period 'al-Mutayyibah'."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until we saw the anger in his face. He was sitting, so he knelt on his knees and said: ""No, no, no. The charity [due] is five [camels], or else ten, or else fifteen, or else twenty, or else twenty-five, or else thirty, or else thirty-five; if they are many, then forty."" He said: ""So they took leave of him, and with the orphan was a stick with which he was striking a camel. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'How great is this stick of an orphan!'"" Hanzalah said: ""So he brought me near to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have sons with beards and younger than that, and this one is the youngest of them, so supplicate Allah for him.' He wiped his head and said: 'May Allah bless you' or 'Blessed be you.'"" Dhayyal said: ""I have indeed seen Hanzalah being brought a person with a swollen face or an animal with a swollen udder; he would spit on his hands, say: 'In the name of Allah,' place his hand on its head and say: 'On the spot of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' then wipe it over it."" Dhayyal said: ""And the swelling would go away."""
"3679","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Dharr that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said: 'Present his minor sins to him.' So they will be presented to him, and his major sins will be hidden from him. It will be said: 'You did such and such on such and such a day,' and he will admit it, not denying it, while fearing the major sins. Then it will be said: 'Give him a good deed in place of every evil deed he did.'"" He said: ""So he will say: 'I have sins which I do not see here.'"" Abu Dharr said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, laugh until his front teeth became visible."
"3680","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Asad bin Kurz that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: ""O Asad bin Kurz! You will not enter Paradise by your deeds, but by the mercy of Allah."" I said: ""Not even you, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Not even me, unless Allah restores me, or Allah envelops me with a mercy from Him."
"3681","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn Abbas that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""O youth of Quraysh! Guard your private parts, do not commit adultery. Verily, whoever guards his private part, for him is Paradise."
"3682","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Aisha that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: ""O Aisha! Beware of the belittled sins, for indeed they have from Allah a pursuer."
"3683","[AI-translation] Hasan as a mursal hadith: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: ""By My Might! I do not gather upon My servant two fears, nor do I gather for him two securities. If he feels secure from Me in the world, I will make him afraid on the Day of Resurrection; and if he fears Me in the world, I will make him secure on the Day of Resurrection."
